    <h1>How this site is built</h1>
    <p class="lede">A portfolio is also a product. These are the decisions behind this one.</p>
    <h2>Content first</h2>
    <p>Every page is plain, semantic HTML generated ahead of time with Eleventy. Everything on it can be read without JavaScript, by people, screen readers, search engines and AI systems alike.</p>
    <h2>No client-side JavaScript</h2>
    <p>Nothing on the site needs it, so none ships. The stylesheet is small enough to inline, and there is one self-hosted variable font, Source Serif 4, for headings. Body text uses the system font.</p>
    <h2>Accessible by default</h2>
    <p>A logical heading order on every page, landmarks, a skip link, visible focus states, color contrast that meets WCAG AA in light and dark mode, and images with dimensions and alt text.</p>
    <h2>Structured for search and answers</h2>
    <p>Each page describes itself with Schema.org data that connects a single Person to the pages, case studies and questions on the site. There’s an XML sitemap, a plain robots.txt, and an <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> summary for language models.</p>
    <h2>Evidence over adjectives</h2>
    <p>Every number on the site names the role it came from. Where a result isn’t measured, the copy says what changed and doesn’t claim a figure.</p>
